# Line endings
#
# Every text blob in this repository is stored with LF endings and is checked
# out with LF endings. This restates in a form git enforces what .editorconfig
# (end_of_line = lf) and the LLVM-based .clang-format style already describe.
#
# The rule is purely protective: as of the last audit no committed text blob
# used CRLF, so turning it on changes no existing content. Without it the
# contract lived only in the editor config, and anything that rewrote the
# working tree with CRLF turned all 664 tracked files into a 203k-line phantom
# diff that buried the 4 files that had actually changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files.
#
# `text=auto` already classifies these correctly today via git's NUL-byte
# sniff (verified: every tracked image trips it), but a binary that happened
# to carry no NUL in its first 8000 bytes would be silently line-ending
# normalised and corrupted. State it instead of trusting the heuristic. The
# PE entries are not hypothetical: .gitignore whitelists sample/**/*.exe and
# sample/**/*.dmp, and the Windows lanes build .obj/.pdb/.dll beside the tree.
*.png binary
*.PNG binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.dmp binary
*.obj binary
*.pdb binary
*.i64 binary
*.vtil binary
*.pdf binary

